    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21491" root="شأف" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِجْلٌ مَشْؤُوفَةٌ</span></b>  <i>A foot affected with an ulcer,</i> or
<i>imposthume, such as is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَأْفَةٌ</span>, <i>breaking out
in it:</i> (O, K:) from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُئِفَتْ رِجْلُهُ</span>. (O, * K, * TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَشْؤُوفٌ</span>, from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شُئِفَ</span>, <i>Frightened,</i> or
<i>afraid;</i> (A'Obeyd, O, K;) applied to a man.
(A'Obeyd, O.)

